msgid "1. The work plan is where you say what you are doing. Not a chat message, not a comment — beans, a committed store any session or agent can read. Claim before you work so a sibling session does not pick up the same item; a bean that turns out not to be wanted is , with its reasons, never deleted."
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:54
msgid "2. Make your first folio. This repository is the platform; your content lives in its own. One command scaffolds it — the manifests, the declaration, the agent files and the link back here:"
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:65
msgid "3. Know which kind of thing you are writing. A document is structured prose; a paper is that plus the block kinds whose assertion is a formal claim, backed by Lean and typeset through LaTeX. The choice decides which blocks are legal and which gates run: Content types."
msgstr ""

#: docs/index.md:70
msgid "4. The documentation you will never read. All of it — the authoring guides, the architecture, the publication workflow, the generated schema and skill reference. It is here, it is thorough, and the honest expectation is that you will arrive at it from a search engine at the exact moment something breaks. That is a fine way to use it. The three steps above are the ones worth reading now."
msgstr ""

